**Network status is not coverage.** Being in-network with a carrier does not mean a
given patient's plan covers a given procedure. Individual benefits are verified by
the office before the visit, every time, and are never confirmed on the phone.

## Cost

Prices are not published and are never quoted on this line. What a visit costs
depends on the patient's coverage and on what the dentist finds at the exam. The
front desk goes through cost with the patient before any treatment is done.

## Clinical questions

This line does not give clinical advice, assess symptoms, recommend medication, or
judge how urgent a problem is. Symptom questions go to the dentist at the visit, or —
for swelling, difficulty breathing or swallowing, fever with swelling, uncontrolled
bleeding, or head trauma — to emergency care and the on-call line immediately.

## What to bring to a first visit

Photo ID, insurance card, and a list of current medications. Patients who want to
fill out new-patient paperwork ahead of time can ask the office to send it.
